From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mvx: quote the MODULE_IMPORT_NS namespace

Building against 7.2 fails with:

  mvx_driver.c:42:18: error: 'VFS_internal_I_am_really_a_filesystem_and_am_NOT_a_driver'
  undeclared here (not in a function)
  mvx_driver.c:43:18: error: 'DMA_BUF' undeclared here (not in a function)

6.13 changed MODULE_IMPORT_NS() to take a string literal rather than a bare
token. This is the same change already carried for the NPU driver in
cix-npu-kmd-1.0/0003-armchina-npu-quote-DMA_BUF-MODULE_IMPORT_NS.patch.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor tree]
The CIX P1 VPU driver is a vendor drop with no upstream submission path;
carried downstream only.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
--- a/driver/mvx_driver.c
+++ b/driver/mvx_driver.c
@@ -39,8 +39,8 @@
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("ARMChina");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Tiube VPU Driver.");
-MODULE_IMPORT_NS(VFS_internal_I_am_really_a_filesystem_and_am_NOT_a_driver);
-MODULE_IMPORT_NS(DMA_BUF);
+MODULE_IMPORT_NS("VFS_internal_I_am_really_a_filesystem_and_am_NOT_a_driver");
+MODULE_IMPORT_NS("DMA_BUF");
 
 static int __init mvx_init(void)
 {
